<!--
  ============================================================================
  Settings: the section list, the cards inside each section, and the Me page's
  settings bodies.

  ## Why this file and not res/values/strings.xml

  `docs/I18N.md`'s rule is 「换哪个文件就抽哪个文件」, and the draw is already
  crowded: several screens are being externalised at once, and one shared file
  would turn every extraction into a merge conflict on the same 200 lines.
  Android merges `res/values/*.xml` by resource *name*, so a second file is a
  file-layout choice with no runtime cost.

  ## Naming

  `settings_<use>`, all lower snake case, and globally unique inside R.string.
  The prefix is the guard: another extraction pass may not reuse a name.

  ## What is deliberately not here

  * the host's own prose — `SettingsChoice.label`, `PermissionOption.name`,
    `AgentPresetOption.name`/`description`, a provider's display name and a
    model's name. Those arrive from `settings/describe` at runtime; a translation
    table over them would translate the deployment's data and stop matching the
    web.
  * a session's title, a workspace's path and its title, and the host's refusal
    message. Same rule: somebody else's words, drawn as received.
  * numbers and units (`API 34`, `12 sp`). Those are formatting, and
    `docs/I18N.md` §4.4 puts them on the number format and the sp value, not on a
    translated sentence.

  ## Where the app's own voice *is* here

  Every other literal in these three files is the app talking: a row label, a
  summary, a section title, an empty state, a failure note this client wrote
  itself. Those are the ones a translator can reach.
  ============================================================================
-->
